hwui's host-flavor registration of every graphics class, as Android registers them (ADR-0043 a2).

The host flavor builds apex/LayoutlibLoader.cpp in place of the device's apex/jni_runtime.cpp. Its
register_android_graphics_classes registers only the classes that layoutlib names in the Java system property
graphics_native_classes, and none without it. Android registers all of its graphics natives when the VM starts,
with no such property. So the function registers every class of LayoutlibLoader's map instead, in the order of
the device's gRegJNI (ColorSpace before Graphics, as jni_runtime.cpp asks). GraphicsJNI::setJavaVM and the
registration itself stay as they are. parseCsv, which only read the property, goes, so that no unused function
meets -Wall and -Werror.

